TOPIC 2: USER MANAGEMENT IN LINUX 
To create a user we use this command 
- useradd username eg. useradd zkari 
however it does not create a home directory for a user or save the details of the user 
To create a user and have it apper in home we use "adduser username"

To set or change a password
- passwd username

To check user passwords 
- cat /etc/shadow

To delete a user
- userdel username 

To check the list of all users 
- cat /etc/passwd

To switch from root to user 
- su - username eg su - zkari

whoami command will prompt your username 
logout will log out of the user and get you back to root 

NB: What is the difference between useradd and adduser?
Both commands do thesame thing but adduser creates a /home directory for the user created. It also takes alot of user information 
while useradd is a quick way of creating a user, it does not ask for details and does not create the home directory 

