How to write to a file in Linux
we first download vim using - apt install vim

VI editor (Vim has 3 modes)
1- Normal mode (used for navigation and command execution)
2-Inset mode (you can write inside a file when you click on i)
3- Command mode (you can save in this mode) 
after writing press escape key and then :wq w is for save and q is for quit 

after that when you type cat filename it will print out the contents of your file 

To navigate within a file first we;
vim filename then switch to normal mode, to switch to normal mode click 0 then :index eg :0 will take you to the first line

cat filename.txt will print everyhing out 
tac filename.txt will print everything out in reverse 

to write to a file we use 
1- echo "content" > filename.txt (this will overrite current file)
2- echo "content" > filename.txt (this will append new content to the bottom of existing file)

